# A constructor function takes its `this` for the object that it is making, whose fields its stores create. Called as a method of a literal it gets an old object: a record is filled by its literal, and a construction makes no record.
# So where every receiver is born by a literal the stores overwrite. f2 = run, with both calls of Point copied in; L1 = the literal.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: = PutSlot {{*}}key="x" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# CHECK: = PutSlot {{*}}key="y" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# RUN(CREATES): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CREATES-NOT: PutSlotOrAdd {{*}}receivers=[L1]
# -- source: a-constructor-function-called-as-a-method-of-a-literal-overwrites-its-fields.cjs
